    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABH7-WVw",
      "title": "feat: add `SetReviewPeriodDelays` template for the per-chain withdrawal delays",
      "author": "0xarktos",
      "number": 1575,
      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nOne `L2TaskBase` template, `SetReviewPeriodDelays`, for the per-chain withdrawal delay setters from ethereum-optimism/optimism#23215 and ethereum-optimism/optimism#23252. It sets `OptimismPortal2.proofMaturityDelaySeconds`, `AnchorStateRegistry.disputeGameFinalityDelaySeconds` and `DelayedWETH.delay` for every chain in the task in one Safe transaction, so an operator signs once for the whole set.\r\n\r\nDraft until the setters are deployed on a Sepolia chain the registry can address.\r\n\r\n## Context\r\n\r\nThe monorepo PRs move the three delays from implementation immutables to per-chain proxy storage with ProxyAdminOwner-only setters bounded by min/max. No template can call them today. After interop migration the ASR and the DelayedWETH are shared by a set while proof maturity stays per portal, so the template is scoped to a whole set and asserts uniform proof maturity across portals sharing an ETHLockbox.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- `src/template/SetReviewPeriodDelays.sol`: every `[delays]` key optional, one value for all chains; bounds check against each contract's min/max at setup; a setter is only called where the on-chain value differs, and a shared ASR or DelayedWETH is written once, so the batch holds exactly the calls for the configured keys (one portal call per chain, one call per shared contract); DelayedWETH resolved from `SystemConfig.delayedWETH()` and registered for the storage allow-list; `_validate` asserts each value per chain, then the per-lockbox uniformity check (isolated in `_checkSetUniformity`).\r\n- `test/template/SetReviewPeriodDelaysToml.t.sol`: no-fork tests for the parser and bounds check.\r\n- `test/tasks/example/sep/044-set-review-period-delays`: example task on sepolia-devnet-2 and -3.\r\n- `test/tasks/Regression.t.sol`: one case, fixture pending.\r\n\r\nInterfaces are declared inline, as the template boilerplate requires.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\n- Setters are not deployed anywhere yet: the example task reverts at `minProofMaturityDelaySeconds()`, so `template_regression_tests` and the regression case fail. After deployment: re-pin the block in `.env` and the test, capture call data and data to sign into the regression case, run `just simulate-all-templates`, un-draft.\r\n- The uniformity check only sees the chains in the task (set membership is not enumerable on-chain), and the policy itself is not confirmed. Dropping it is deleting `_checkSetUniformity`.\r\n- Confirm the `Supports:` versions against the release tag.\r\n\r\nCloses [#697](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism-private/issues/697)\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-12T09:41:14Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-23T14:41:25Z",
      "additions": 878,
